Note: Auth API — user registration and login with real password hashing
Note: Run with: epl run examples/official_starters/auth_api/main.epl
Note: Test:     curl http://localhost:8080/api/health
Note:
Note: Passwords are hashed with auth_hash_password (never stored in plain text)
Note: and checked with auth_verify_password. Login issues a random session token
Note: from auth_generate_token. Every query is parameterized ("?") so usernames
Note: can't be injected.

Display "Starting Auth API..."
db = db_open("auth_api.db")
db_execute(db, "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, username TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL, password_hash TEXT NOT NULL)")

Note: ── Helpers ──
Function find_user takes username
    Return db_query_one(db, "SELECT id, username, password_hash FROM users WHERE username = ?", [username])
End

Function register_user takes username, password
    If length(username) < 3 Then
        Return Map with ok = False and error = "Username must be at least 3 characters"
    End
    If length(password) < 6 Then
        Return Map with ok = False and error = "Password must be at least 6 characters"
    End
    If find_user(username) == nothing Then
        hashed = auth_hash_password(password)
        db_execute(db, "INSERT INTO users (username, password_hash) VALUES (?, ?)", [username, hashed])
        token = auth_generate_token(48)
        Return Map with ok = True and user = username and token = token
    Otherwise
        Return Map with ok = False and error = "Username already exists"
    End
End

Function login_user takes username, password
    account = find_user(username)
    If account == nothing Then
        Return Map with ok = False and error = "Invalid credentials"
    End
    If auth_verify_password(password, account.password_hash) Then
        token = auth_generate_token(48)
        Return Map with ok = True and user = account.username and token = token
    Otherwise
        Return Map with ok = False and error = "Invalid credentials"
    End
End

Create webapp app

Note: ── Health check ──
Route "/api/health" responds with
    Send json Map with status = "ok" and service = "epl-auth-api" and version = "1.0.0"
End

Note: ── Register  (body: {"username": "...", "password": "..."}) ──
Route "/api/register" responds with
    data = web_request_data()
    Send json register_user(trim(data["username"]), data["password"])
End

Note: ── Login  (body: {"username": "...", "password": "..."}) ──
Route "/api/login" responds with
    data = web_request_data()
    Send json login_user(trim(data["username"]), data["password"])
End

Say "Auth API running at http://localhost:8080"
Start app on port 8080
